<title>BULGARIA: Greek Ionian Bank Bulgaria branch back in profit.</title>
<headline>Greek Ionian Bank Bulgaria branch back in profit.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sofia branch of Greece's Ionian bank posted 312.8 million lev net profit for 1996, of which 16.7 million levs were set aside to cover the 1995 loss, the bank's balance sheet published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Ionian Bank Sofia branch annual results follow in million levs unless stated otherwise: *</p>
<p>						 1996	  1995</p>
<p>Total revenue			 4,954.540	24.894</p>
<p>Net interest income on lev</p>
<p>transactions			   -498.937	-2.047</p>
<p>Net interest income on foreign</p>
<p>currency transactions		  31.645	 9.149</p>
<p>Net income on securities trading  964.964	 0.094</p>
<p>Foreign currency</p>
<p>translation gains		     113.425	-0.887</p>
<p>Business and administration costs 125.206	23.292</p>
<p>Taxes				     208.612	   0.0</p>
<p>Profit				    312.765     -16.727</p>
<p>Total assets			  7,315.677     360.835</p>
<p>Cash				    1,512.917     330.819</p>
<p>Interbank deposits extended     4,814.978	10.000</p>
<p>Attracted interbank deposits	208.570	90.302</p>
<p>Attracted deposits from</p>
<p>non-financial clients	     5,936.215	63.669</p>
<p>Lending to non-financial clients	0.0	   0.0</p>
<p>Treasury portfolio		    926.100	10.000</p>
<p>Non-financial assets		   31.063	27.014</p>
<p>Items not included</p>
<p>in the balance **		   2,768.982	 2.335</p>
<p>* Under local banking regulations branches of foreign banks are not required to have equity capital paid in and to set aside provisions against risk assets.</p>
<p>** Under local accountancy standards items that are not included in the balance involve bank guarantees issued by the bank and other commitments. -- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
